# prereqs

you need [zine](https://zine-ssg.io) (ssg written in zig) and node 18+.
easiest path is nix: run `nix-shell`, shell.nix brings everything (node,
the zine binary, pillow for og images).

no nix? grab nodejs, build zine from source, `pip install pillow`.

# start

```bash
git clone https://codeberg.org/scclie/notizine.git my-site
cd my-site
npm install
npm run dev      # localhost:1987
```

# make it yours

1. `host_url` in zine.ziggy -> your real domain
2. flip flags in assets/notizine.ziggy, see [config](/notes/config/)
3. delete demo stuff in content/, or drop a locale from zine.ziggy
4. move sidebar widgets around in slots, same file

# ship it

```bash
npm run build    # output in public/
```

drop public/ on any static hosting: codeberg pages, github pages,
nginx. `npm run preview` serves it locally with proper 404 fallback.
